Nuked CQM: the modulation and the output without shifting a negative number

Three places scale a signed sample with a left shift, which is undefined
behaviour when the sample is negative. UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the
program at the first of them, a few milliseconds into a note:

  src/chips/nuked_cqm/cqm.c:277:57: runtime error: left shift of negative value
  -510

* The modulation of the next operator is the previous output, scaled by 4.

* doshifter() scales its argument when the shift is more than 12. The
  modulation, which is what reports, arrives there with a shift of 13 or 15, so
  a factor of 2 or 8; its other callers pass the frequency number, which is not
  negative. The C89 form of doshifter() is a macro and the C99 form a function;
  both change.

* The output of the chip is the wave sample, scaled by 32 before doshifter()
  scales it back down.

Multiplications say the same thing and are defined. What is scaled here is a
chip sample or a frequency number, hundreds of thousands at the very most, so
every product is far inside an int.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/nuked_cqm/cqm.c b/src/chips/nuked_cqm/cqm.c
index 475032d..9dbfe9a 100644
--- a/src/chips/nuked_cqm/cqm.c
+++ b/src/chips/nuked_cqm/cqm.c
@@ -145,11 +145,11 @@ enum {
 static inline int doshifter(int x, int shift)
 {
     if (shift > 12)
-        return x << (shift - 12);
+        return x * (1 << (shift - 12));
     return x >> (12 - shift);
 }
 #else
-#   define doshifter(x, shift) (shift > 12 ? (x << (shift - 12)) : (x >> (12 - shift)))
+#   define doshifter(x, shift) (shift > 12 ? (x * (1 << (shift - 12))) : (x >> (12 - shift)))
 #endif
 
 void CQM_Generate(cqm_t* chip, int16_t* sample)
@@ -274,7 +274,7 @@ void CQM_Generate(cqm_t* chip, int16_t* sample)
             modptr[1] = 0;
         }
         else if (op != 0)
-            modptr[chip->oddeven ^ 1] = chip->wave_prev << 2;
+            modptr[chip->oddeven ^ 1] = chip->wave_prev * 4;
 
         {
             int wf;
@@ -797,7 +797,7 @@ void CQM_Generate(cqm_t* chip, int16_t* sample)
 
             if (chip->dooutput && !(chip->is4op2 && !con))
             {
-                int sumwave = doshifter(chip->wavesample << 5, chip->waveshift);
+                int sumwave = doshifter(chip->wavesample * 32, chip->waveshift);
 
                 if (chip->wavepan & 1)
                     accum[0] += sumwave;
